Analysis only, NOT applied by build-hakios-metal.sh (darwin-lisa session 9, 2026-11-12): does CoreAnimation's
framebuffer fetch ever only blend? Applies over the hakios-metal-*.patch series in userland/ (after
hakios-metal-x-ubwc-rt.patch).

compiler.cpp fetchToBlend: between ir3_finalize_nir and lowerFbRead, colour 0 of a fragment stage is followed back
through the NIR from its store; when every channel is A + B * dst.same-channel (A and B free of the destination,
dst the framebuffer fetch of colour 0) the stage is rewritten to output A, and B as the second source when it is not
the 1 - A.a of source-over, and Program::fetchBlend tells the draw to blend ONE, ONE_MINUS_SRC_ALPHA or ONE, SRC1_*.
compileStage takes it as FETCH_TO_BLEND; tools/sweep.cpp -b compiles one function so, and HM_FETCHBLEND_DUMP=1 prints
the decision and the NIR.

Result over QuartzCore 26's default.metallib (arm64 slice), the 46 constant sets of fixed_frag_lph_cph found in the
logs and every *_lph fragment function: none converts. The draws that blend plainly (fc_blend_function 29=62) do not
fetch at all (fbRead 0: CoreAnimation gives them the pipeline's blend); the ones that fetch unpremultiply the
destination (dst.rgb / max(dst.a, 1e-4)), run a 4x4 colour matrix over it and clamp it (29=43, 29=50), read the clip's
SDF attachment (path_blit, 55=2), branch on the destination (p3_clamp, edr_clamp, color_edr,
alpha_linear_premultiply) or square it (luma_boost, edr_scale). So no fixed-function blend can take their place, and
a copy of the target read as a texture costs a full-screen copy more than the fetch it replaces.

Use: apply this over the series in a copy of hakios-metal, `make MESA=1 out/host-mesa/sweep`, then
`HM_FETCHBLEND_DUMP=1 out/host-mesa/sweep -b -f fixed_frag_lph_cph -c 5=2 -c 29=43 ... qc.metallib` (qc.metallib: the
first slice of QuartzCore.framework/default.metallib, bytes 48..1551232).

